> I'm not sure I am the best person to ask.  I tend to learn by reading
> source materials (source code, technical papers, etc) rather than text
> books, so I have no experience of reading a RAID text book and finding
> it useful or not.  Possibly others on the list might have experiences
> they could share.
> 
> However, having said that, I can recommend
> 
>   Managing RAID on Linux
> by Derek Vadala, published by  O'Reilly
> 
> I know about it because I helped with the technical review.
> It is reasonably well balanced with general introduction material,
> some technical details, and some practical sys-admin guidelines.
> It is certainly an adequate text, and may well be a very good text.
